Positive Behavioral Change: To manage the acute compartmentalization fatigue, enforce a strict 48-hour "boundary of silence": decline all incoming communications and social requests without providing an explanation or education; visually checking off these declined interactions on a notepad will positively reinforce the right to exist without explaining oneself. To safely rebuild energy, implement a "low-demand sensory routine": engage only with familiar, non-challenging media (e.g., re-watching a favorite childhood movie) for 30 minutes twice daily; this provides predictable, safe input that demands zero identity negotiation.
Home-Based Services (Optional): Referral to a specialized intersectional psychotherapist.
DME/Safety (Optional): None.
Follow-up: Routine GP review within 3-5 days to monitor energy levels and coordinate appropriate, culturally safe psychological care.

